"A **hexagonal number** is a figurate number that is a hexagon in a triangular lattice. The formula for the $ n $-th hexagonal number is:\n\n$$\nH_n = n(2n - 1)\n$$\n\nThis formula can be derived from the geometric properties of hexagonal numbers.\n\n### Function Definition:\n\n```python\ndef hexagonal_num(n):\n    return n * (2 * n - 1)\n```\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert hexagonal_num(10) == 190\nassert hexagonal_num(5) == 45\nassert hexagonal_num(7) == 91\n```\n\n### Explanation of the Test Cases:\n\n- For $ n = 10 $:  \n  $ H_{10} = 10 \\times (2 \\times 10 - 1) = 10 \\times 19 = 190 $\n\n- For $ n = 5 $:  \n  $ H_5 = 5 \\times (2 \\times 5 - 1) = 5 \\times 9 = 45 $\n\n- For $ n = 7 $:  \n  $ H_7 = 7 \\times (2 \\times 7 - 1) = 7 \\times 13 = 91 $\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n```python\ndef hexagonal_num(n):\n    return n * (2 * n - 1)\n```"
